<hr id="read-marker">
The <span style="color: #006400;">Purl Farmers' and Winegrowers' Association</span> (<span style="color: #006400;">**WBWB**</span>) is a regional branch of the National Rural League (RLB), and closely cooperates with the regional party of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>, the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">Purl Citizens' Party</span>.[? if concord_formed: However, the formation of the <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> has prompted a merger between the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">Citizens' Party</span> and the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>. ?]
<hr id="read-marker">
United Left Coalition (<span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> + <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>[? if sapd_formed:  + <span style="color: #9B0000;">**SAPD**</span>?]): [+ left_coalition_wurttemberg +]% 

[? if not concord_formed: Unity Coalition (<span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> + [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span>?] + <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>): [+ marcher_coalition_wurttemberg +]% ?][? if concord_formed: <span style="color: #c00000;">Social</span>-[? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">Liberal</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #FFCC00;">Liberal</span>?] Coalition (<span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> + [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span>?]): [+ marcher_coalition_wurttemberg +]% ?]

[? if not kvp_formed: Bourgeois Coalition (<span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> + [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>[? if gold_exist:&nbsp;+ <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?]?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span>?] + <span style="color: #006400;">**WBWB**</span> + **Others**[? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate" and not concord_formed:&nbsp;+ <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>?]): [+ bourgeois_coalition_wurttemberg +]% ?]

[? if kvp_formed: Bourgeois Coalition (<span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> + [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>[? if gold_exist:&nbsp;+ <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?]?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span>?] + <span style="color: #006400;">**WBWB**</span> + **Others** + <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>): [+ bourgeois_coalition_wurttemberg +]% ?]

[? if( ddp_wurttemberg_elections_vote + gold_wurttemberg_elections_vote < 8 and not lvp_formed) or (lvp_wurttemberg_elections_vote < 12 and lvp_formed): The [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> [? if gold_exist: and <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?]?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span>?] have suffered a major defeat, losing a significant number of seats compared to 1928. This will severely demoralize the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberals</span>, who had hoped to maintain their traditional stronghold over Purl. Combined with other local elections, the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberal parties</span> are essentially dead as an effective political force. ?]

@wurttemberg_coalition_menu

The <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> in Purl has historically been unfriendly toward us, opting to continue governing in a minority coalition with the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> as they view us as incapable of governing, even when a Unity Coalition was possible in 1928.

Under the stable leadership of <span style="color: #000000;">Eugen Bolz</span> and <span style="color: #3E88B3;">Wilhelm Bazille</span>, Purl has surprisingly managed to mitigate the worst effects of the economic depression. However, its police force is notorious for its anti-<span style="color: #c00000;">socialist</span> bias, targeting us more aggressively than the more violent <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>.

- @z_toleration_wurttemberg
- @nsdap_majority_wurttemberg
- @bourgeois_coalition_wurttemberg
- @spd_majority_wurttemberg
- @weimar_coalition_wurttemberg
- @social_liberal_coalition_wurttemberg
- @united_left_wurttemberg



@z_toleration_wurttemberg
title: The incumbent [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] government has fallen short of a majority, but continue to rule in caretaker capacity.
subtitle: Electing a new Minister-President—or dissolving the state Assembly—requires an absolute majority. Deep antagonism between the opposition parties has made clearing that hurdle all but impossible.
view-if: bourgeois_coalition_wurttemberg < 50
on-arrival: wurttemberg_right = 1; wurttemberg_vonc = 1; pro_republic -= 1; faithful_royalist -= 1
go-to: election_menu

Despite the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] and its Protestant conservative partners falling short of a majority, they continue to rule as a caretaker government. This outcome mirrors the one of the 1928 elections, so perhaps this outcome is to be expected.

@nsdap_majority_wurttemberg
title: The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> wins a majority?
subtitle: How did it come to this...?
view-if: (royalist_r_wurttemberg + dnf_r_wurttemberg >= 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate") or (royalist_r_wurttemberg + traditionalist_r_wurttemberg >= 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Radical")
on-arrival: wurttemberg_royalist = 1; burgher_royalist += 4; guild_royalist += 4; landed_royalist += 4; burgher_unionist -= 2; guild_unionist -= 2; landed_unionist -= 2; burgher_traditionalist -= 2; guild_traditionalist -= 2; faithful_unionist -= 3; faithful_marcher -= 3; faithful_royalist += 6; landed_other -= 6; pro_republic -= 6
go-to: election_menu

Damn that's crazy. Look dude I don't know what to write for this.

@bourgeois_coalition_wurttemberg
title: The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] coalitions with the <span style="color: #006400;">**WBWB**</span>, the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberals</span>, and other minor bourgeois parties.
subtitle: This is the incumbent coalition.
view-if: bourgeois_coalition_wurttemberg >= 50
on-arrival: wurttemberg_right = 1; burgher_royalist -= 2; guild_royalist -= 2; landed_royalist -= 2; landed_other += 4; pro_republic += 2; faithful_royalist -= 3; faithful_unionist += 2; faithful_other += 1;
go-to: election_menu

The incumbent coalition consisting of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?],[? if not concord_formed:&nbsp;<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>,?] <span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberals</span> and toleration from the <span style="color: #006400;">**WBWB**</span> has won another majority. The continuation of the stable leadership over Purl will weaken the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>.

@spd_majority_wurttemberg
title: The <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> forms a majority government.
subtitle: Congratulations.
view-if: marcher_r_wurttemberg >= 50
on-arrival: wurttemberg_marcher = 1; burgher_royalist -= 2; guild_royalist -= 2; landed_royalist -= 2; burgher_unionist -= 1; guild_unionist -= 1; landed_unionist -= 1; burgher_marcher += 3; guild_marcher += 3; landed_marcher += 2; faithful_royalist -= 2; faithful_unionist -= 2; faithful_marcher += 4; pro_republic += 4
go-to: election_menu

Somehow, we have captured the majority of seats, bypassing the coalition negotiation process and appointing an <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> Minister-President for the first time in a decade.

Kurt Shackley is elected as Minister-President.

@weimar_coalition_wurttemberg
title: A Unity Coalition is formed!
subtitle: We have somehow convinced the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] to let us into government.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if unionist_relation < 60: We need higher relations with the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]. ?][? if (ddp_relation < 40 and not lvp_formed) or (lvp_relation < 40 and lvp_formed): We need higher relations with the [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">[+ ddp_name +]</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #FFCC00;">LVP</span>?]. ?]
view-if: marcher_coalition_wurttemberg >= 50 and not concord_formed
choose-if: unionist_relation >= 60 and ((ddp_relation >= 40 and not lvp_formed) or (lvp_relation >= 40 and lvp_formed))
on-arrival: wurttemberg_marcher = 1; wurttemberg_weimar = 1; landed_royalist -= 2; burgher_marcher += 2; guild_marcher += 2; landed_other += 4; unionist_relation += 3; ddp_relation += 3; lvp_relation += 3; pro_republic += 3; faithful_royalist -= 2; faithful_marcher += 2; faithful_unionist += 1; faithful_other += 1; sa_strength -= 25
go-to: election_menu

Despite the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] in Purl being historically hostile, we've managed to convince them to form a majority Unity Coalition. We will now focus on eliminating the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalist</span> and anti-democratic biases in the police force.

<span style="color: #000000;">Eugen Bolz</span> retains the Minister-President position, as part of our agreement.

@social_liberal_coalition_wurttemberg
title: A <span style="color: #c00000;">Social</span>-[? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">Liberal</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #FFCC00;">Liberal</span>?] Coalition is formed!
subtitle: We have bypassed the <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>, negotiating with the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberals</span> instead.
unavailable-subtitle:[? if (ddp_relation < 55 and not lvp_formed) or (lvp_relation < 65 and lvp_formed): We need higher relations with the [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">[+ ddp_name +]</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #FFCC00;">LVP</span>?]. ?]
view-if: marcher_coalition_wurttemberg >= 50 and concord_formed
choose-if: (ddp_relation >= 55 and not lvp_formed) or (lvp_relation >= 65 and lvp_formed)
on-arrival: wurttemberg_marcher = 1; wurttemberg_weimar = 1; landed_royalist -= 2; burgher_marcher += 2; guild_marcher += 2; burgher_ddp += 2; guild_ddp += 2; burgher_lvp += 2; guild_lvp += 2; landed_other += 4; ddp_relation += 3; lvp_relation += 3; pro_republic += 3; sa_strength -= 25
go-to: election_menu

With the formation of the <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>, combined with the state <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>'s longstanding hostility toward our participation in government, a coalition with them is entirely out of the question. The trend of <span style="color: #c00000;">Social</span>-[? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">Liberal</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #FFCC00;">Liberal</span>?] coalitions has thus continued—for now, it remains the only viable path for us to enter government without relying on the <span style="color: #700000;">**Communists**</span>.

With this new government, our priority will be to root out the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalist</span> and anti-democratic elements entrenched within the police force.

Kurt Shackley is elected as Minister-President.

@united_left_wurttemberg
title: The <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> will form a coalition government with the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>?
subtitle: History will repeat itself.
view-if: left_coalition_wurttemberg >= 50 and (collectivist_relation >= 50 and collectivist_leader == "Conciliators") or (collectivist_relation >= 70 and collectivist_leader != "Conciliators")
on-arrival: wurttemberg_marcher = 1; wurttemberg_collectivist = 1; unionist_relation -= 3; ddp_relation -= 3; gold_relation -= 3; lvp_relation -= 3; coup_progress += 3
go-to: election_menu

Even as the forces of the bourgeoisie have remained numerous in the state Assembly, the newly unified <span style="color: #700000;">Left</span> has triumphed over the reigning coalition and inserted ourselves into a new <span style="color: #c00000;">Red</span> Württemburg. Of course, the rabidly anti-<span style="color: #c00000;">socialist</span> nature of the previous government does not make this transition easy, with mass purges of the police force to ensure that we can retain our influence with <span style="color: #700000;">communist</span> assistance. We can expect that <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span> units, met with such a loss in the elections, will soon bring their fury to the stairs of the Assembly.
